/-
# Dense-stage compiler for the physical BF4 graph-norm limit

The preceding graph-norm limit bridge asks for finite representatives and for
convergence of both their norms and their transferred norms.  This file
factors that interface through literal dense observables.

At scale `s`, a continuum Cauchy representative `X` is sampled at an explicit
index and mapped into the finite physical BF4 carrier.  Two exact
intertwining laws identify its finite macro transfer with the pointwise
continuum time shift.  Consequently one Type-level `ModCauchyEv` norm modulus
also controls the transferred norm, after applying it to `TCauchy X`; the
second convergence law is proved rather than assumed.

The dense-stage map, diagonal modulus, vacuum-complement preservation, and
limit pin are still analytic inputs.  No continuum measure, thermodynamic
limit, or Clay mass-gap theorem is constructed here.
-/

import YMGap.Continuum.BF4PhysicalModulatedGapLimitStability
import YMGap.Continuum.SummableCRealEventualStepVariation

namespace YMGap.Continuum.BF4PhysicalDenseStageGraphNormCompiler

set_option maxRecDepth 100000
set_option maxHeartbeats 5000000

open YMGap.Constructive
open YMGap.Continuum
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4MatchedPhysicalAFBridge
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4PhysicalMarkovGNSCompletion
open YMGap.Continuum.BF4PhysicalMarkovModulusCompletion
